WEBVTT

01:12.640 --> 01:19.180
THAT TIME I GOT REINCARNATED AS A SLIME

01:41.500 --> 01:45.500
EPISODE 66: THE FLOOD OF VISITORS

01:50.140 --> 01:52.050
With the Founder's Festival
coming close,

01:52.050 --> 01:54.850
my schedule was fully packed.

02:02.270 --> 02:04.100
King Blumund, huh.

02:04.730 --> 02:08.490
As always, he looks like a character
straight from children's picture books.

02:10.180 --> 02:12.110
I apologize for not thanking you sooner.

02:12.570 --> 02:17.200
Thank you for helping us out
in dealing with Falmuth.

02:17.700 --> 02:20.370
Please, don't mind it, Sir Rimuru.

02:20.370 --> 02:22.580
There's no need to thank me.

02:22.580 --> 02:25.670
I was simply living up to our treaty.

02:25.670 --> 02:28.340
And I'm sure Fuze already told you this.

02:28.340 --> 02:32.130
I entrusted the fate
of my nation to you.

02:32.130 --> 02:34.760
And of course, I do stand for profit.

02:34.760 --> 02:37.220
So there's no need
for you to thank me.

02:37.560 --> 02:39.970
Still, you believed in us.

02:40.390 --> 02:42.350
I appreciate that.

02:44.440 --> 02:49.980
Is it safe to say that our treaty
remains in effect, then?

02:50.390 --> 02:52.070
Of course.
I couldn't ask for more.

02:52.470 --> 02:54.990
May our partnership continue
for many years to come.

02:56.530 --> 02:59.780
Also, I heard the news from Fuze.

02:59.780 --> 03:04.500
He told me you're doing some
grand project right now.

03:04.500 --> 03:09.290
Well, that's something involving more
beyond just your nation and mine.

03:09.290 --> 03:12.380
I'm hoping to gather the representatives
from all nations involved

03:12.380 --> 03:14.920
and explain the details first.

03:16.300 --> 03:19.050
Come on,
a little spoiler won't hurt, right?

03:19.050 --> 03:21.060
Just a quick rundown, then.

03:21.600 --> 03:25.810
I want Blumund to become
a central distribution hub in the future.

03:31.690 --> 03:34.570
I see, that is indeed grand.

03:34.570 --> 03:41.470
Your Majesty, we must make this project
a complete success at all costs.

03:41.470 --> 03:42.830
Indeed.

03:42.830 --> 03:44.790
My wife is right.

03:44.790 --> 03:49.790
Sir Rimuru, thank you
for the delightful proposal.

03:49.790 --> 03:53.340
We shall be on our way now.

03:53.920 --> 03:58.590
I hope the Founder's Festival
is a resounding success.

03:58.590 --> 04:00.090
Thank you very much.

04:00.090 --> 04:02.980
I hope you enjoy your stay in our nation.

04:05.270 --> 04:07.440
Well, Rimuru, here I am.

04:09.980 --> 04:13.690
I'm exhausted from my first journey
by carriage in years, I'll have you know.

04:15.490 --> 04:18.450
All because of you,
I have tons of stuff to deal with.

04:18.450 --> 04:23.450
And I can't just go far on a Pegasus alone
for an official state visit.

04:25.160 --> 04:28.000
I see.
Sounds like a lot of work.

04:28.000 --> 04:32.210
I heard the highway from Blumund
was pretty packed right now, too.

04:32.210 --> 04:36.260
I should develop trains soon
to make transportation more comfortable.

04:36.260 --> 04:39.720
By the way, Rimuru.
I heard you fought Hinata.

04:40.090 --> 04:44.220
The words say it ended in a draw,
but you actually won, right?

04:44.220 --> 04:45.810
Oh, you figured that out?

04:45.810 --> 04:48.600
So, what are you up to this time?

04:50.020 --> 04:53.230
Well, even if you ask me that...

04:53.230 --> 04:54.480
What are you talking about?

04:54.480 --> 04:56.360
Don't give me that.

04:57.070 --> 04:59.860
The Western Holy Church went to us

04:59.860 --> 05:05.370
and formally asked to open
a channel for future negotiations.

05:05.370 --> 05:11.460
They used to consider us creatures
only a step away from monsters,

05:11.460 --> 05:13.610
but they suddenly changed their mind.

05:14.130 --> 05:16.880
I bet this is one of your doings.

05:16.880 --> 05:18.630
Oh, yeah, now that you mention it!

05:18.630 --> 05:22.640
I did involve Dwargon in our
hundred-year friendship treaty

05:22.640 --> 05:25.130
while I proposed to the Crusaders.

05:28.270 --> 05:29.990
Why didn't you tell me?

05:37.230 --> 05:39.150
I see.

05:39.570 --> 05:43.660
So the Seven Days Clergy was behind
their human supremacy policy, huh.

05:47.700 --> 05:50.960
Yeah, and it seems
the Crusaders are thinking about

05:50.960 --> 05:53.830
purging those poisoned
by the Seven Days' thinking.

05:54.420 --> 05:56.170
Now that their leader is gone,

05:56.170 --> 05:59.670
I believe Hinata will seize the Church
in its entirety.

05:59.670 --> 06:01.050
I bet so.

06:01.470 --> 06:05.550
It is foolish to turn down this offer, then.

06:06.020 --> 06:08.310
I knew you would say that.

06:08.310 --> 06:12.520
Enough from you. You always go off
and do stuff without my permission.

06:12.520 --> 06:17.110
But oh well. No need to be a stick
in the mud during this festive occasion.

06:18.300 --> 06:21.070
I'll just enjoy what you've got for me.

06:21.470 --> 06:22.360
Please do!

06:22.360 --> 06:24.030
Hinata will be coming too,

06:24.030 --> 06:27.200
so I'm thinking of setting us up
a room to talk after the festival.

06:27.200 --> 06:30.700
All right. I'll let my companions
know about that too.

06:30.700 --> 06:32.870
I'm sure they'll be shocked
to hear that, though.

06:32.870 --> 06:33.660
Huh?

06:33.660 --> 06:34.710
Oh, I see...

06:37.710 --> 06:39.500
Long time no see, Rimuru.

06:39.500 --> 06:41.960
As promised, I became a king too.

06:41.960 --> 06:45.220
The suit does make the man, eh?

06:45.220 --> 06:46.970
I hope for our continued partnership.

06:48.260 --> 06:50.140
I should be the one saying that, pal!

06:50.640 --> 06:54.140
You're the one who took me
all the way up to king.

06:54.640 --> 06:57.230
So I hope you'll see this to the end.

06:58.360 --> 07:01.320
The long-standing kingdom
of Falmuth had fallen.

07:02.690 --> 07:06.660
In its place now is a new kingdom
born out of menace,

07:06.660 --> 07:08.990
giving its name "Falmenace."

07:08.990 --> 07:13.580
And likewise, its king, Youm,
styles himself as Youm Falmenace.

07:15.020 --> 07:17.080
I apologize
for not introducing myself sooner.

07:17.520 --> 07:21.590
I am the wife of King Youm Falmenace,
Mjur Falmenace.

07:22.010 --> 07:24.510
I look forward to
our continued partnership.

07:24.510 --> 07:27.510
You really look
the part of a queen, Mjurran.

07:27.510 --> 07:28.720
I know, right?

07:28.720 --> 07:31.100
She's well-educated and all, unlike me.

07:32.600 --> 07:35.690
As surprising as it might be,
I have some experience in this.

07:35.690 --> 07:38.900
Clayman was really picky
about manners and etiquette.

07:38.900 --> 07:41.900
I suppose any experience
is worth something.

07:41.900 --> 07:45.740
That's always a problem for me,
I tell you.

07:45.740 --> 07:50.030
Just a while ago, I had to greet
every tribe in the forest of Jura.

07:50.030 --> 07:53.290
I had to just sit straight for hours
like a statue. It's such a work.

07:53.290 --> 07:55.580
Yeah, I hear ya.

07:55.580 --> 07:59.290
I got all these nobles requesting
an audience with me left and right.

07:59.710 --> 08:04.260
Just thinking about some idiots trying to
start faction wars is giving me headache.

08:04.760 --> 08:07.800
And you became the head
of the knight corps, eh?

08:07.800 --> 08:10.050
I did reject the offer.

08:10.050 --> 08:12.560
But this guy just won't listen.

08:12.980 --> 08:17.810
Even now I still consider myself a member
of Lord Carrion's Animal King's Brigade.

08:18.170 --> 08:22.190
Though, I suppose I'll have to
babysit this moron for now.

08:22.190 --> 08:24.000
Shut up, you're the moron!

08:24.000 --> 08:25.250
What did you say, moron Youm!

08:25.250 --> 08:26.570
You're more of a moron than me!

08:26.570 --> 08:27.820
What?! What?!

08:27.820 --> 08:30.660
Please! Lord Youm! Captain Grucius!

08:30.660 --> 08:33.490
You're being terribly rude
in front of Demon Lord Rimuru!

08:33.490 --> 08:35.200
Edgar...

08:35.200 --> 08:36.630
You're always so serious.

08:37.870 --> 08:39.330
C'mon, why not?

08:39.330 --> 08:43.500
He's more put-together than you.
Couldn't ask more for a crown prince.

08:43.500 --> 08:45.380
Captain Grucius, please!

08:45.380 --> 08:47.670
Now is not the time for jokes!

08:47.670 --> 08:49.970
I'm trying my best to serve
as Lord Youm's attendant

08:49.970 --> 08:53.850
to make sure he becomes a good king!

08:53.850 --> 08:55.640
So you're Edgar, huh?

08:56.430 --> 08:59.100
You're King Edmaris's son, right?

08:59.100 --> 09:00.520
Y-Yes, sir!

09:00.520 --> 09:02.150
A former king, that is.

09:02.610 --> 09:04.960
I'm sure it's hard work,
but I'm counting on you.

09:08.110 --> 09:12.450
Now then, since you fulfilled your promise,
I have a present for you.

09:12.950 --> 09:14.030
Diablo.

09:14.030 --> 09:15.450
Yes, Great Rimuru.

09:16.080 --> 09:17.200
Here it is.

09:23.000 --> 09:24.880
Rimuru, this is...

09:24.880 --> 09:29.050
Y-You're forgiving the rest
of the reparations?!

09:29.050 --> 09:33.550
Yeah. Now that Youm is the king,
we don't need that anymore.

09:33.940 --> 09:37.310
And as a matter of fact,
we already received 1,500 stellars.

09:37.310 --> 09:38.720
Hold on!

09:38.720 --> 09:40.730
That means you're making Lord Youm a king

09:40.730 --> 09:43.840
who haggled reparations
from a Demon Lord?!

09:45.170 --> 09:48.320
This'll surely add more stellar story
to your reputation, right, Youm?

09:49.900 --> 09:54.870
I don't quite get it,
but if you say so, then I bet it will.

09:55.700 --> 09:58.330
Well then,
let's grab a drink or two next time.

09:58.790 --> 10:00.330
Let's go, guys.

10:05.710 --> 10:10.010
Now that I've got some free time,
I went to Engrassia.

10:11.220 --> 10:13.400
Long time no see, Rimuru!

10:13.400 --> 10:15.340
Sounds like you've
been through a lot, huh?

10:15.790 --> 10:17.890
That's all you've got to say?

10:17.890 --> 10:21.930
I got attacked by Hinata,
my nation got invaded by Falmuth,

10:21.930 --> 10:25.020
and then the Demon Lords summoned me.

10:25.020 --> 10:27.690
It's a barrage of one thing
after another.

10:27.690 --> 10:31.150
The word "a lot" doesn't
even begin to describe it.

10:32.400 --> 10:35.200
Still, not even all of that
is enough to take you down.

10:35.200 --> 10:39.450
I managed to make up with Hinata,
so I suppose it all ended well.

10:39.450 --> 10:40.580
I'm glad to hear that.

10:41.080 --> 10:44.750
I met her a few times
to exchange information,

10:44.750 --> 10:48.250
and I was sure I told her
what kind of person you are.

10:48.250 --> 10:51.090
But you know,
Hinata is very suspicious of people.

10:51.090 --> 10:54.760
Yeah, she really doesn't listen
to what other people say.

10:54.760 --> 10:56.140
Right?

10:56.140 --> 10:59.850
She's the type who only believes
in things she sees for herself.

10:59.850 --> 11:03.140
You won't believe how much problem
I got because of it.

11:04.710 --> 11:06.270
So what do you say?

11:06.270 --> 11:08.690
If you're busy,
I won't force you,

11:08.690 --> 11:11.530
but would you like to check
the festival for two or three days?

11:13.240 --> 11:15.400
Of course I'm going!

11:15.400 --> 11:18.070
That's why I tried so hard
to get ahead in my work!

11:19.490 --> 11:24.620
And I also have a reliable staff I feel safe
to leave this place to while I'm gone.

11:25.790 --> 11:27.170
Let me introduce her to you.

11:27.170 --> 11:31.170
This is Kagali,
the vice-master of Free Guild.

11:31.170 --> 11:33.840
Hello, Demon Lord Rimuru.

11:33.840 --> 11:36.010
It is an honor to meet you.

11:36.010 --> 11:37.680
Nice to meet you.

11:37.680 --> 11:40.100
I came here before,
but we haven't met, I believe?

11:41.010 --> 11:43.020
Yes, you wouldn't have been able to.

11:43.020 --> 11:46.270
I've only returned here recently.

11:48.310 --> 11:50.400
My passion is exploring old ruins.

11:50.810 --> 11:57.400
I've just come back from mapping out Soma,
one of the largest ancient ruins in the west.

11:58.310 --> 12:03.870
A portion of the sales of items
excavated from the ruins goes to Kagali.

12:03.870 --> 12:05.500
Hm, I see.

12:05.500 --> 12:07.670
So you can make money
from ruins, huh?

12:08.140 --> 12:11.250
In my case,
it was simply part of my hobby.

12:11.250 --> 12:16.670
I have auctioned off things I excavated
in the past to pay for my expenses.

12:16.670 --> 12:21.640
Just a question, but who's got
the rights to the ruins?

12:22.050 --> 12:25.180
Is it whatever nation
they're located in?

12:25.180 --> 12:28.140
Hmm, that's a hard question to answer.

12:28.570 --> 12:30.340
In the case of Soma for example,

12:30.340 --> 12:34.650
it's managed by Free Guild,
but the location is making it a bit tricky.

12:35.150 --> 12:38.820
It was discovered in a desert region
called the Barren Lands,

12:38.820 --> 12:42.320
farther west
from Western Nations territory.

12:42.320 --> 12:47.620
The Barren Lands is right up against
the domain of the Demon Lord Daggrull.

12:47.620 --> 12:52.670
So everyone's too afraid
to claim the land as theirs.

12:52.670 --> 12:57.590
So as a matter of fact,
nobody currently has rights to the ruin.

12:57.590 --> 12:59.170
I see.

12:59.170 --> 13:04.470
We'll have to be careful
with that too, then.

13:04.470 --> 13:06.680
Hm? Is something bothering you?

13:06.680 --> 13:11.190
There's actually a ruin
at Clayman's headquarters.

13:11.190 --> 13:13.940
What did you say? Is that true?

13:13.940 --> 13:19.740
I think he harnessed
the things he found in that ruin.

13:19.740 --> 13:21.070
But the thing is...

13:24.200 --> 13:29.670
This might be rude to say in front of someone
who makes exploring ruins their profession...

13:30.330 --> 13:34.710
But I don't like the idea of
plundering ruins just for the treasures.

13:36.360 --> 13:39.970
I want to know
how the people there used to live,

13:39.970 --> 13:42.130
what kind of culture they had,

13:42.130 --> 13:45.220
and why their cities fell.

13:45.220 --> 13:47.650
I want to know all those things first.

13:48.610 --> 13:50.390
So we don't let the past go to waste,

13:50.390 --> 13:54.060
I think we need to at least give
that much respect to the ancient people.

13:54.060 --> 13:57.570
Oh, you're surprisingly
quite a romanticist, huh?

13:57.570 --> 13:59.650
What do you mean by "surprisingly"?

13:59.650 --> 14:02.700
I'm a man who got some romance in him,
I'll have you know.

14:03.200 --> 14:04.820
True.

14:04.820 --> 14:07.530
You'd have to be, to come up
with the idea of building

14:07.530 --> 14:10.330
a nation of monsters yourself.

14:10.330 --> 14:12.410
I see.

14:12.410 --> 14:15.380
That is a perspective I did not have.

14:15.960 --> 14:17.960
But I can empathize with it.

14:17.960 --> 14:23.930
I am not a fan of seeing ruins
get vandalized myself.

14:24.430 --> 14:29.720
As for Clayman's domain, I've been
left in charge of managing it, so...

14:29.720 --> 14:31.890
I'm very interested.

14:31.890 --> 14:35.850
Would you allow me to pay
that ruin a visit someday?

14:35.850 --> 14:36.730
Yeah, of course.

14:36.730 --> 14:39.320
I've been planning to
investigate it one day,

14:39.320 --> 14:42.860
and I was thinking of consulting
about it with an expert like you.

14:42.860 --> 14:44.990
It'd be great if you could come along.

14:44.990 --> 14:48.020
Yes, it'll be a pleasure!

14:53.000 --> 14:56.330
So you're going to get
the kids to the festival, too?

14:56.330 --> 14:57.380
Yeah.

14:57.380 --> 15:01.760
We already made up with Hinata,
so there should be no one in our way now.

15:01.760 --> 15:06.430
We've got security all around the area,
so the kids should be safe.

15:06.430 --> 15:07.680
Okay.

15:07.680 --> 15:10.850
They're taking their studies
more seriously lately,

15:10.850 --> 15:14.590
so giving them their due break
and reward would be nice.

15:15.140 --> 15:16.810
Seriously, huh...

15:17.270 --> 15:20.570
That must mean Ms. Tiss
is being liked by the kids.

15:21.090 --> 15:24.650
Hey, kids! You all doing well...

15:24.650 --> 15:27.160
Sensei! What took you so long?!

15:27.160 --> 15:32.160
She's right! You promised you'd
show your face once in a while!

15:32.160 --> 15:36.120
We were worried you
had forgotten about us.

15:36.120 --> 15:39.920
But I'm glad you came, Sensei.

15:42.090 --> 15:44.570
Welcome back, Sensei!

15:48.140 --> 15:50.350
Oh, Yuuki-oniichan is here!

15:50.350 --> 15:51.930
Yuuki-niichan!

15:51.930 --> 15:54.150
You're gonna fight me
like you promised, right?!

15:54.150 --> 15:54.890
Me too!

15:54.890 --> 15:56.270
Right!

15:56.270 --> 16:00.110
We've gotten better at handling
our elemental power lately.

16:01.020 --> 16:03.980
You'd need to train another
hundred years to beat me!

16:03.980 --> 16:06.900
I can fight you if you want,
but not today.

16:06.900 --> 16:08.530
Aww, why?!

16:08.530 --> 16:11.830
It's a shame,
but we don't have much time today.

16:11.830 --> 16:12.990
What do you mean?

16:12.990 --> 16:17.160
I wanted to invite you all
to my nation today!

16:17.160 --> 16:19.220
We're holding a big festival tomorrow.

16:19.220 --> 16:21.040
But well, if you don't wanna go...

16:21.040 --> 16:22.960
Hurry! We gotta get ready!

16:22.960 --> 16:24.090
Got it, Ken-chan!

16:24.090 --> 16:27.720
Aww, you should tell us something
that important ahead of time!

16:27.720 --> 16:31.640
She's right! How could you
tell us that without warning?

16:32.640 --> 16:35.390
Um, I can't wait!

16:35.390 --> 16:37.730
All you need to bring is
a change of clothes, okay?

16:37.730 --> 16:39.230
Okay!

16:39.230 --> 16:41.270
It's been a while, Mr. Rimuru.

16:41.770 --> 16:43.480
Ms. Tiss!

16:43.480 --> 16:46.110
You're as popular with the kids as always.

16:46.110 --> 16:48.030
Makes me a little jealous.

16:48.030 --> 16:49.360
Don't be like that.

16:49.360 --> 16:53.450
You're the only one I can feel at ease
leaving those five with.

16:53.450 --> 16:55.290
I'm glad you think so highly of me...

16:55.950 --> 17:01.790
But to be honest, the kids are so strong,
I don't have much left to teach them.

17:02.920 --> 17:05.800
I can teach them ways to fight
back in my nation,

17:05.800 --> 17:11.050
but I think you're the only one who can
teach them how to grow as a person.

17:11.050 --> 17:12.390
Mr. Rimuru...

17:14.690 --> 17:16.270
Sorry for the wait.

17:16.270 --> 17:18.680
Huh? Where's your stuff, Ms. Tiss?

17:18.680 --> 17:19.350
What?

17:19.350 --> 17:21.600
You should come with us.

17:21.600 --> 17:22.690
That's right!

17:22.690 --> 17:24.750
It's okay right, Mr. Rimuru?

17:25.650 --> 17:26.730
You heard them.

17:27.690 --> 17:29.200
Ms. Tiss.

17:30.400 --> 17:32.260
I'll go get my stuff!

17:44.710 --> 17:48.050
Sorry, but I still have
some work left to do.

17:48.050 --> 17:51.470
So I think I can only
meet you guys at night.

17:51.470 --> 17:52.510
WHAT?!

17:52.510 --> 17:53.470
Quiet!

17:53.470 --> 17:56.720
So I'm thinking you can play
a game using this.

17:57.760 --> 18:02.770
This serves as a free pass ticket for
the stalls that'll open at the festival.

18:03.480 --> 18:07.400
With this, you can freely eat
and drink stuff from any of the stalls,

18:07.900 --> 18:10.650
and you can go to any
event venue you like.

18:10.650 --> 18:14.530
But you only have
a budget of 100 gold coins!

18:14.530 --> 18:17.160
If you used it all up,
it's a game over.

18:17.660 --> 18:21.580
When that happens, you have to go back to
your room and do homework as a punishment.

18:21.580 --> 18:23.170
What do say? Game on?

18:23.170 --> 18:24.170
I'll do it!

18:24.170 --> 18:27.540
I bet there's all this rare stuff to see.
Can't wait, huh, Ken-chan?

18:27.540 --> 18:28.960
Yeah, I can't wait!

18:28.960 --> 18:30.710
Thank you, Sensei!

18:30.710 --> 18:34.050
Um, we'll buy you some presents!

18:35.970 --> 18:38.810
There's no festival without allowance!

18:38.810 --> 18:41.060
And of course,
free time to explore!

18:41.060 --> 18:45.630
By the way, most of the stalls only sell stuff
that's priced less than 1 gold coin.

18:45.630 --> 18:48.980
So it'll be more difficult to actually
use up all 100 gold coins in 3 days.

18:48.980 --> 18:52.400
It's a game in name only.
Just an excuse to give them money.

18:52.400 --> 18:53.490
Great Rimuru.

18:53.490 --> 18:57.450
Hero Masayuki and his party have
arrived on the outskirts of the town.

18:57.450 --> 18:58.490
He's finally here...

18:59.700 --> 19:00.990
Hero...

19:00.990 --> 19:04.000
Now then, what kind of guy he'll be...

19:14.260 --> 19:16.220
You must be Demon Lord Rimuru.

19:16.720 --> 19:19.510
To think you'd go
out of your way to greet us.

19:19.950 --> 19:22.470
Lord Masayuki is a renowned hero.

19:22.470 --> 19:25.230
Not even a Demon Lord
could afford to ignore him.

19:26.770 --> 19:28.520
What do you say, Masayuki?

19:28.520 --> 19:30.690
Should we settle things
right here and now?

19:31.530 --> 19:34.530
They sure are saying
all the stuff they want.

19:34.980 --> 19:38.370
Well, well.
The hero's party sure is harsh.

19:38.370 --> 19:40.910
As my thanks for bringing back the elves,

19:40.910 --> 19:43.290
you are all free to enter
and stay in the town.

19:43.290 --> 19:47.540
If you like, I can prepare you a house,
so feel free to stay as long as you want.

19:47.540 --> 19:51.920
But I have no intention of
"settling things" here, okay?

19:53.800 --> 19:57.970
I knew it! It seems this Demon Lord
is afraid of Masayuki!

19:57.970 --> 20:01.350
I heard you're seeking friendship
with us humans,

20:01.350 --> 20:03.680
but can't say we can trust you so easily.

20:03.680 --> 20:07.020
Perhaps you've managed
to trick Saint Hinata well enough,

20:07.020 --> 20:10.810
but don't expect you can be so lucky
with Masayuki here.

20:10.810 --> 20:13.650
You sure are hell-bent
on making me the bad guy.

20:13.650 --> 20:16.390
Hmph, the evil must perish!

20:16.390 --> 20:19.740
Lord Masayuki, let's take down this
Demon Lord right away and bring peace...

20:19.740 --> 20:22.410
What are you guys doing?

20:22.410 --> 20:23.910
Oh, Yuuki!

20:23.910 --> 20:26.830
Well, well, if it isn't Yuuki.

20:26.830 --> 20:31.670
The head of the Free Guild himself
keeping tabs on a Demon Lord?

20:31.670 --> 20:33.040
No, I'm not.

20:33.040 --> 20:35.460
I'm telling you,
Rimuru here truly wishes

20:35.460 --> 20:38.010
to form a friendly relationship
with us humans.

20:38.010 --> 20:41.050
The fact that you guys are
still alive here is proof of that.

20:41.050 --> 20:42.930
What do you mean by that?

20:42.930 --> 20:44.390
From the way you phrase it,

20:44.390 --> 20:48.310
it sounds like you're saying Masayuki
is weaker than Saint Hinata.

20:48.310 --> 20:50.190
Don't you underestimate us.

20:50.190 --> 20:53.060
A mere Demon Lord is no match
for Lord Masayuki!

20:53.060 --> 20:56.130
I won't let you make a fool of
Masayuki like that.

20:56.130 --> 20:58.610
I dunno how strong this
Hinata chick is supposed to be,

20:58.610 --> 21:02.070
she's only strong enough to get a draw
with that Demon Lord over there anyway.

21:02.480 --> 21:05.870
In that case, it's time for the headliner
to make his debut, ain't it?

21:05.870 --> 21:07.450
Hey, calm down.

21:07.450 --> 21:11.080
Like I told you, Rimuru is not our enemy.

21:11.080 --> 21:13.210
There's no reason for us to fight.

21:13.210 --> 21:16.300
But still, that guy's a Demon Lord.

21:16.300 --> 21:19.130
Who knows when he might carry out
his nefarious scheme!

21:19.130 --> 21:21.720
Now that the Western
Holy Church chickening out,

21:21.720 --> 21:26.060
ain't it about time Masayuki shows
everyone what he can do as a Hero?

21:26.060 --> 21:28.140
No, I'm telling you...

21:28.140 --> 21:29.430
All right.

21:29.430 --> 21:31.140
In that case, I've got a proposal.

21:31.620 --> 21:35.360
We'll be holding a battle tournament
at the festival starting tomorrow.

21:35.900 --> 21:41.660
And if you guys participate and emerge
a champion, I'll accept your challenge.

21:42.090 --> 21:44.030
Not a bad offer, right?

21:44.030 --> 21:47.660
Oh, so you want to embarrass yourself
right in front of the masses?

21:48.050 --> 21:50.290
What do you say, Masayuki?

21:50.290 --> 21:52.170
We should accept this proposal.

21:52.170 --> 21:54.960
To further spread your good reputation,

21:54.960 --> 21:58.630
let's carry out justice right in front of
the people you must protect!

21:58.630 --> 22:01.420
Yeah, um, you're right.

22:01.930 --> 22:05.350
All right. I'll accept that proposal.

22:05.350 --> 22:08.180
Whoa, are you sure about this, Masayuki?

22:09.680 --> 22:12.440
I think things will work out,
like it always is.

22:12.440 --> 22:16.560
Well, since it's a tournament,
I doubt there'll be any killing.

22:16.560 --> 22:18.780
Just watch out, okay?

22:18.780 --> 22:21.150
Heh, do you even know
who you're talking to?

22:21.150 --> 22:23.490
Let's go, Masayuki.

22:23.490 --> 22:26.990
To prepare for tomorrow,
let's take it slow and rest.

22:27.460 --> 22:32.250
With so many onlookers,
I doubt Demon Lord can do anything funny.

22:32.250 --> 22:37.960
Don't worry! I'll keep a close eye on any
attempt at poisoning or assassination!

22:37.960 --> 22:39.880
A-Anyway, let's go!

22:39.880 --> 22:42.670
We'll need to check out
when the tournament begins tomorrow.

22:44.300 --> 22:46.850
Seems like yet another problem
to deal with.

22:46.850 --> 22:48.810
Well, whatever happens, happens.

22:49.140 --> 22:51.850
I suppose I'll just think
about it positively that

22:51.850 --> 22:56.310
having a Hero in my tournament's
going to give it a mark of prestige.

22:57.810 --> 23:02.490
And like that, a Hero suddenly
entered my tournament.

24:36.000 --> 24:38.500
Next time,
"The Eve of the Festival."
